WF-52 — Slack Channel Manager

## Summary

- Inputs: phone_number (or phoneNumber), name (or userName), userId
- Outputs: Returns { success, channelId, channelName, channelUrl }. Creates a new private Slack channel `consult-<phoneNumber>` and invites the admin user (U0AGTECS1KR), OR if the channel already exists, returns the existing channel.
- State Transitions: none (caller — WF-22 — persists slack_channel_id to users row)
- Calls Sub-Workflows: none

---

## Algorithm

Step 1: Start — triggered by another workflow (typically WF-22) with { phone_number, name, userId } passed through.
Step 2: Prepare channel name (code): channelName = `consult-<phoneNumber>`. Carry userName, phoneNumber, userId forward. Go to Step 3.
Step 3: Create private Slack channel via Slack API (conversations.create, name=channelName, is_private=true). On error use the error output branch.
  - On success → go to Step 4 (new-channel branch).
  - On error → go to Step 6 (error branch).
Step 4: Invite admin to the new channel via Slack API (conversations.invite, channel=<new channel id>, users=['U0AGTECS1KR']). Go to Step 5.
Step 5: Build new-channel return (code): { success:true, channelId=<new id>, channelName=<new name>, channelUrl=`https://app.slack.com/client/<team_id>/<channel_id>` }. Go to Step 10.
Step 6: Check: does the error message contain 'name_taken'?
  - If YES → go to Step 7
  - If NO → end with error (no further handling).
Step 7: List all private channels via Slack API (conversations.list, types=private_channel, returnAll=true). Go to Step 8.
Step 8: Filter that list for the one whose name equals the prepared channelName. Go to Step 9.
Step 9: Build existing-channel return (code): { success:true, channelId=<existing id>, channelName=<existing name>, channelUrl=`https://app.slack.com/client/<team_id>/<channel_id>` }. Go to Step 10.
Step 10: End (return object emitted to caller).
